# vault-broker.env — secret/config env drop-in for the rc.d service.
# Install to /usr/local/etc/terrapi-vault/vault-broker.env  (mode 0600, root:vault).
# The rc.d script sources this so secrets never appear in `ps` argv. Values that
# read `$(cat <dataset path>)` are expanded at service start from the unlocked
# ZFS-encrypted dataset — NEVER commit real secrets.

# --- Residency + listeners ---------------------------------------------------
# Per-instance constant; eu and uae NEVER co-reside (residency.md).
VAULT_RESIDENCY_GROUP=eu
# Broker API: mTLS-over-WireGuard, WG /32 only, never ext_if. (eu example IP.)
VAULT_BROKER_BIND=10.200.0.101:8200
# Prometheus metrics: WG /32 (on-box Prometheus is a separate jail → not loopback).
VAULT_METRICS_BIND=10.200.0.101:8201

# --- Crown-jewel state (on the ZFS-encrypted dataset, mode 600) --------------
VAULT_STORE_PATH=/var/db/terrapi-vault/store.sqlcipher
VAULT_AUDIT_PATH=/var/db/terrapi-vault/audit.jsonl
VAULT_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/var/db/terrapi-vault/snapshots
# Unattended unseal: a mode-600 passphrase file on the encrypted dataset.
VAULT_UNSEAL_PASSPHRASE_FILE=/var/db/terrapi-vault/unseal.pass

# --- Arm (a): identity-sealed master key (KMS root-of-trust) -----------------
# OPTIONAL. Set VAULT_IDENTITY_KMS_URL to unseal the master key via identity's WG-only
# native-mTLS KMS listener instead of (augmenting) the passphrase above — a stolen at-rest
# store is then inert without a live in-group call to identity (secrets-broker.md §KMS root).
# Absent ⇒ manual passphrase only. If identity is unreachable at boot, the broker falls back
# to VAULT_UNSEAL_PASSPHRASE[_FILE] (break-glass). Auth is mTLS: the broker presents its OWN
# VAULT_TLS_CERT/KEY (must be the dot-form clientAuth cert vault.<group>.proximi.internal) and
# trusts identity's server cert via VAULT_TLS_CLIENT_CA (fleet Root CA) — no app-layer secret.
# One-time bootstrap: run once with VAULT_KMS_SEAL_INIT=1 to seal the current passphrase +
# write the blob, then unset.
# VAULT_IDENTITY_KMS_URL=https://10.200.0.100:8202
# VAULT_SEALED_MASTER_FILE=/var/db/terrapi-vault/sealed-master.json   # default: next to the store
# VAULT_KMS_SEAL_INIT=1   # one-time only — seals VAULT_UNSEAL_PASSPHRASE[_FILE] under identity, then remove
# On an identity ROOT rotation the broker re-seals its master under the new root (at boot + on this
# timer) and emits B3 kms.master_resealed so identity retires the old root. Root rotation is annual,
# so the default 6h is ample; lower only if you need faster pickup within identity's overlap window.
# VAULT_KMS_RESEAL_CHECK_SECS=21600

# --- mTLS material (fleet Root CA; server cert + client-CA bundle) -----------
VAULT_TLS_CERT=/usr/local/etc/terrapi-vault/tls/server.pem
VAULT_TLS_KEY=/usr/local/etc/terrapi-vault/tls/server.key
VAULT_TLS_CLIENT_CA=/usr/local/etc/terrapi-vault/tls/fleet-root-ca.pem

# --- Role/capability authz (REQUIRED in prod — absent ⇒ every cert 403) ------
# SAN(dNSName) → {role, caps}. Shape: deploy/roles.json.sample.
VAULT_ROLES_CONFIG=/usr/local/etc/terrapi-vault/roles.json

# --- KMS root-of-trust: identity-minted JWT for the `kms` cap (Option J) ------
# OPTIONAL. Set the issuer to require an identity-minted short-TTL ES256 bearer JWT
# as the per-call `kms` cap proof (ON TOP of mTLS) — secrets-broker.md §KMS root-of-trust.
# Absent ⇒ kms ops stay cap-based (cert-SAN `kms` capability; the aether path).
# Pin the issuer per group, EXACT incl. trailing slash; verifier enforces aud="vault",
# scope ⊇ kms, residency_group == VAULT_RESIDENCY_GROUP, and tenant_id == path tenant.
# VAULT_KMS_JWT_ISSUER=https://identity.eu.proximi.fi/
# VAULT_KMS_JWT_AUDIENCE=vault                      # default "vault" if unset
# VAULT_KMS_JWT_JWKS_URI=https://identity.eu.proximi.fi/.well-known/jwks.json  # else OIDC-discovered

# --- OpenSearch: TWO distinct creds (least privilege) ------------------------
# (a) Dynamic-cred ENGINE — needs a privileged security-API cred to mint/delete
#     ephemeral internal users + assign the audit-writer security role. NOT the
#     write-only audit-writer. Infra mints a dedicated least-priv user
#     (e.g. vault-credmgr) scoped to internalusers management.
VAULT_OS_URL=https://opensearch.eu.internal:9200
VAULT_OS_ADMIN_USER=vault-credmgr
VAULT_OS_ADMIN_PASSWORD=$(cat /var/db/terrapi-vault/secrets/os-credmgr.pass)
# (b) Audit SHIP — bulk-index the broker's own B3 events to audit-events-{group}-*.
#     Reuses the existing WRITE-ONLY audit-writer cred.
VAULT_AUDIT_OS_URL=https://opensearch.eu.internal:9200
VAULT_AUDIT_OS_USER=audit-writer
VAULT_AUDIT_OS_PASSWORD=$(cat /var/db/terrapi-vault/secrets/audit-writer.pass)
# TLS trust for these OpenSearch clients (rustls; they do NOT use the FreeBSD system trust).
# For a fleet-CA-signed OS node cert, point these at the fleet Root CA (PEM) — when set, that CA
# is the SOLE trust root and the cert verifies (preferred over the insecure toggle below).
# VAULT_OS_CA=/usr/local/etc/terrapi-vault/tls/fleet-root-ca.pem
# VAULT_AUDIT_OS_CA=/usr/local/etc/terrapi-vault/tls/fleet-root-ca.pem
# Dev/self-signed clusters only — NEVER in prod with a real CA (use the *_OS_CA option instead):
# VAULT_OS_INSECURE_TLS=1
# VAULT_AUDIT_OS_INSECURE_TLS=1

# --- Object-store presign (DO Spaces tile publish/serve) ---------------------
# OPTIONAL. Set VAULT_OBJECT_STORE_KEY to enable the presign ops: publish (`object-store`
# cap → presigned PUT, consumer outer-map) + serve (`object-store-read` cap → presigned GET,
# consumer belt). Absent ⇒ both ops return 503 not_configured. The broker holds ONE
# long-lived per-group Spaces RWD key (operator-created in the DO control panel — DO has no
# key API), uses it ONLY to compute SigV4 signatures, and NEVER returns it; the per-tenant /
# write-only / single-object scoping lives in each signed URL (secrets-broker.md
# §Object-store presign). Key/secret live on the encrypted dataset, never in argv.
# VAULT_OBJECT_STORE_KEY=$(cat /var/db/terrapi-vault/secrets/spaces.key)
# VAULT_OBJECT_STORE_SECRET=$(cat /var/db/terrapi-vault/secrets/spaces.secret)
# VAULT_OBJECT_STORE_REGION=fra1
# VAULT_OBJECT_STORE_BUCKET=proximi-outermap-eu
# Virtual-hosted host; default <bucket>.<region>.digitaloceanspaces.com. Override for S3/MinIO.
# VAULT_OBJECT_STORE_HOST=proximi-outermap-eu.fra1.digitaloceanspaces.com
# Presigned-URL lifetime: default 300 s, hard max 900 s (requested ttl_secs clamped to [1,max]).
# VAULT_OBJECT_STORE_TTL_SECS=300
# VAULT_OBJECT_STORE_MAX_TTL_SECS=900

# --- Request hardening (ALL optional; safe defaults shown) -------------------
# Defensive limits for the API surface. The broker is WG-only + mTLS with a handful
# of trusted daemon principals, so these are DoS-resistance guards, not public-traffic
# throttles. Uncomment to override; absent ⇒ the built-in default applies.
# VAULT_MAX_BODY_BYTES=65536        # max request body (413 over this); bodies are tiny JSON
# VAULT_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECS=15     # per-request time budget (408 on overrun)
# VAULT_MAX_CONCURRENCY=256         # global in-flight cap (503 when saturated)
# VAULT_RATE_PER_SEC=50             # sustained per-principal (per mTLS SAN) rate, tokens/s
# VAULT_RATE_BURST=100              # per-principal burst depth (429 when exhausted)
